IMPORT prelude

-- Treasurer of Presbyterian Church, Singapore Ordinance 1899 (Singapore) -- who the Corporation "The Treasurer of the Presbyterian
-- Church in Singapore" is and when a new Treasurer qualifies (ss 2(1), 4), what the Ordinance empowers it to do (s 2(2), (3)), how its
-- deeds are sealed and signed (s 3), the replacement of the old trustees by the Corporation as sole trustee (s 5), the land vested in
-- it and on what estate and trusts (ss 6, 7 and the two Schedules), and whose rights the Ordinance leaves alone (s 8).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/TPCSO1899.txt. The deposit says the edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The only amendment
-- annotation in the body is "[7/97]" under s 8. The Ordinance is dated 29 December 1899.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0244 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance (historical, private and spent Acts). It asks what the Ordinance decides for a person or business it applies to; no
-- scenario has asked a sharper question yet. The Ordinance has eight sections and two Schedules, so all of it except the short title is
-- in scope. For a person outside the congregation it matters when dealing with the Corporation over land (ss 2(3), 3, 4), and for the
-- holders of the 31 building leases on the First Schedule land (s 6).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1 (short title); the content of s 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886, to which s 3(1) refers (whether a
-- power of attorney was "deposited" under it is a stated fact); the terms of the 1879 indenture and the 1892 Statutory Land Grant
-- beyond what the preamble recites (the trusts are named, not encoded); the boundaries in the Schedules (only the areas are encoded);
-- what office "the office of the Minister of the Colony" in s 4(1) now means.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Treasurer of Presbyterian Church, Singapore Ordinance 1899 -- the Corporation`

§§ `2(1) and 4 -- who is the Corporation, and when a new Treasurer is duly qualified`

-- s 2(1): "Francis Warrack and his successors for the time being in the office of Treasurer of the said congregation, duly qualified as
-- hereinafter provided, shall be a body corporate, hereinafter called the Corporation", named "The Treasurer of the Presbyterian
-- Church in Singapore", with perpetual succession and a corporate seal.
-- s 4(1): "No successor of the said Francis Warrack in the office of Treasurer ... shall be deemed to be duly qualified as aforesaid
-- unless and until he has caused an extract from the minutes of the Board of Managers of the said congregation appointing him such
-- Treasurer, certified as correct by the Chairman of the Board, to be filed in the office of the Minister of the Colony, and unless and
-- until a notification of such filing has appeared in the Gazette."
-- s 4(2): "Such notification shall be sufficient evidence of the appointment and that the person named therein is duly qualified".
--
-- All four steps are needed: appointment by the Board of Managers, an extract of the minutes certified by the Chairman, its filing, and
-- the Gazette notification. The preamble says the Treasurer "is appointed by the Board of Managers"; the appointment is a stated fact.
DECLARE Treasurer HAS
    `is appointed Treasurer by the Board of Managers` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the extract of minutes is certified by the Chairman` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certified extract is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `notification of the filing has appeared in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the treasurer` IS A Treasurer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is duly qualified under section 4` IF
        `the treasurer`'s `is appointed Treasurer by the Board of Managers`
    AND `the treasurer`'s `the extract of minutes is certified by the Chairman`
    AND `the treasurer`'s `the certified extract is filed`
    AND `the treasurer`'s `notification of the filing has appeared in the Gazette`

-- s 2(1): only a successor "duly qualified" is the Corporation.
GIVEN `the treasurer` IS A Treasurer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the Corporation` IF
    `is duly qualified under section 4` `the treasurer`

-- s 4(2): the Gazette notification is sufficient evidence of appointment and qualification. It is evidence, not a further condition.
GIVEN `the treasurer` IS A Treasurer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Gazette is sufficient evidence of qualification` IF
    `the treasurer`'s `notification of the filing has appeared in the Gazette`

§§ `2(2) and 2(3) -- what the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to do`

-- s 2(2): "The said seal may from time to time be broken, changed, altered and made anew as the Corporation thinks fit."
-- s 2(3): "The Corporation may acquire, purchase, take, hold and enjoy movable and immovable property of every description, and may
-- sell, convey, assign, surrender and yield up, mortgage, demise, reassign, transfer or otherwise dispose of any movable and immovable
-- property vested in the Corporation upon such terms as the Corporation thinks fit."
--
-- Disposal reaches only property "vested in the Corporation". The Ordinance contains no words
-- letting the Corporation sue or be sued; the Ordinance grants no such power (whether the general law supplies one is not encoded).
DECLARE Power IS ONE OF
    `break, change or make anew its seal`
    `acquire or purchase property`
    `hold and enjoy property`
    `sell property`
    `mortgage property`
    `demise property`
    `surrender property`
    `sue or be sued`
    `borrow money without security`

GIVEN `the power` IS A Power, `the property is vested in the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `break, change or make anew its seal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `acquire or purchase property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `hold and enjoy property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sell property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `mortgage property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `demise property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `surrender property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3 -- sealing and signing the Corporation's instruments`

-- s 3(1): instruments "requiring the seal of the Corporation shall be sealed with the seal of the Corporation in the presence of the
-- said Francis Warrack or his attorney duly authorised by a power of attorney deposited under section 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of
-- Property Act 1886, or in the presence of his successor for the time being in the said office of Treasurer or his attorney duly
-- authorised as aforesaid, and shall also be signed by the said Francis Warrack or his said attorney or by his said successor or his
-- said attorney."
-- s 3(2): "Such signing shall be sufficient evidence of the due sealing of such deeds, documents and other instruments."
--
-- Three things must all be true: the seal, its affixing in the presence of the Treasurer or a deposited attorney, and the signature of
-- the Treasurer or a deposited attorney. Witness and signer need not be the same person on the words; that reading is encoded.
-- s 3 speaks of the successor "for the time being in the said office", without the words "duly qualified"; whether a Treasurer not yet
-- gazetted under s 4 can witness and sign is not settled by s 3 itself. This encoding reads s 3 with s 2(1) and requires the
-- Treasurer to be duly qualified: an inference, flagged in NOTES.md.
DECLARE Officer IS ONE OF
    `the duly qualified Treasurer`
    `an attorney of the Treasurer under a deposited power of attorney`
    `an attorney whose power of attorney is not deposited`
    `a Treasurer appointed but not yet gazetted`
    `the Chairman of the Board of Managers`
    `nobody`

DECLARE Instrument HAS
    `is sealed with the Corporation seal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sealed in the presence of` IS AN Officer
    `signed by` IS AN Officer

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the Treasurer or a deposited attorney` IF
    CONSIDER `the officer`
    WHEN `the duly qualified Treasurer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an attorney of the Treasurer under a deposited power of attorney` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is executed as section 3 requires` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `is the Treasurer or a deposited attorney` (`the instrument`'s `sealed in the presence of`)
    AND `is the Treasurer or a deposited attorney` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`)

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signature is sufficient evidence of due sealing` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `is the Treasurer or a deposited attorney` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`)

§§ `5 -- the Corporation replaces the trustees`

-- s 5(1): "The persons now trustees of the said indenture of 14 February 1879, and of the Statutory Land Grant of 16 August 1892, are
-- hereby removed from their offices of trustees."
-- s 5(2): "The Corporation is hereby appointed sole trustee of the said instruments in place of them notwithstanding the provisions
-- contained in the said instruments, providing against the number of the trustees thereof not being less than 2, and the powers of
-- appointing new trustees contained in the said instruments are hereby cancelled."
DECLARE TrustInstrument IS ONE OF
    `the 1879 indenture`
    `the 1892 Statutory Land Grant`
    `some other trust instrument`

GIVEN `the trust instrument` IS A TrustInstrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5 governs it` IF
    CONSIDER `the trust instrument`
    WHEN `some other trust instrument` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the trust instrument` IS A TrustInstrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Corporation is sole trustee of` IF
    `section 5 governs it` `the trust instrument`

GIVEN `the trust instrument` IS A TrustInstrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a new trustee may be appointed under the instrument's own power` IF
    NOT (`section 5 governs it` `the trust instrument`)

GIVEN `the trust instrument` IS A TrustInstrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the minimum of 2 trustees still binds` IF
    NOT (`section 5 governs it` `the trust instrument`)

GIVEN `was a trustee in 1899` IS A BOOLEAN, `the trust instrument` IS A TrustInstrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is removed as trustee by section 5` IF
    `was a trustee in 1899` AND `section 5 governs it` `the trust instrument`

§§ `6, 7 and the Schedules -- the land vested in the Corporation`

-- s 6: the First Schedule land is "vested for the respective residues of the said terms of 999 years ... in the Corporation, subject to
-- the payment of the rents and to the observance and performance of the covenants and conditions contained in the leases mentioned in
-- the First Schedule, and subject also to the said 31 indentures of leases, but nevertheless upon the trusts contained in the said
-- indenture of 14 February 1879."
-- s 7: the Second Schedule land "is hereby vested in the Corporation for an estate in fee simple, but nevertheless upon the trusts
-- contained in the said Statutory Land Grant of 16 August 1892."
-- First Schedule, item 1: bounded by North Bridge Road and Cross Street "now called Bras Basah Road", "containing 3085.7 m2", demised
-- 30 September 1828 "for the term of 999 years". Item 2: also on Bras Basah Road, "containing an area of 1063.7 m2", demised 14 June
-- 1832 for 999 years. Second Schedule: bounded by "Orchard Road, now called Stamford Road", "containing by admeasurement 7208.5 m2".
DECLARE Parcel IS ONE OF
    `First Schedule item 1 (North Bridge Road)`
    `First Schedule item 2 (Bras Basah Road)`
    `Second Schedule (Stamford Road church land)`
    `land not in either Schedule`

DECLARE Estate IS ONE OF
    `the residue of a 999-year term`
    `fee simple`
    `nothing`

DECLARE Trusts IS ONE OF
    `the trusts of the 1879 indenture`
    `the trusts of the 1892 Statutory Land Grant`
    `no trusts under the Ordinance`

GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH AN Estate
DECIDE `the estate vested in the Corporation` IS
    CONSIDER `the parcel`
    WHEN `First Schedule item 1 (North Bridge Road)` THEN `the residue of a 999-year term`
    WHEN `First Schedule item 2 (Bras Basah Road)` THEN `the residue of a 999-year term`
    WHEN `Second Schedule (Stamford Road church land)` THEN `fee simple`
    OTHERWISE `nothing`

GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A Trusts
DECIDE `the trusts it is held on` IS
    CONSIDER `the parcel`
    WHEN `First Schedule item 1 (North Bridge Road)` THEN `the trusts of the 1879 indenture`
    WHEN `First Schedule item 2 (Bras Basah Road)` THEN `the trusts of the 1879 indenture`
    WHEN `Second Schedule (Stamford Road church land)` THEN `the trusts of the 1892 Statutory Land Grant`
    OTHERWISE `no trusts under the Ordinance`

-- s 6: the First Schedule land is vested "subject also to the said 31 indentures of leases".
GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the vesting is subject to the 31 building leases` IF
    CONSIDER `the parcel`
    WHEN `First Schedule item 1 (North Bridge Road)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `First Schedule item 2 (Bras Basah Road)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the area in square metres` IS
    CONSIDER `the parcel`
    WHEN `First Schedule item 1 (North Bridge Road)` THEN 3085.7
    WHEN `First Schedule item 2 (Bras Basah Road)` THEN 1063.7
    WHEN `Second Schedule (Stamford Road church land)` THEN 7208.5
    OTHERWISE 0

-- The year each 999-year head lease began, from the First Schedule (1828 and 1832); 0 where there is no such term.
GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the year the 999-year term began` IS
    CONSIDER `the parcel`
    WHEN `First Schedule item 1 (North Bridge Road)` THEN 1828
    WHEN `First Schedule item 2 (Bras Basah Road)` THEN 1832
    OTHERWISE 0

-- When the 999-year term would run out, counted from the year in the Schedule: arithmetic on the Schedule's figures, not a date the
-- Ordinance states.
GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the year the 999-year term runs out` IS
    IF `the year the 999-year term began` `the parcel` EQUALS 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the year the 999-year term began` `the parcel` + 999

§§ `Preamble -- the 31 building leases and the reverter (recited, not enacted)`

-- Preamble: Thomas Dunman "subdivided the same into 31 building allotments, which he demised by 31 indentures of lease unto certain
-- lessees for terms of 99 years, reserving to himself the yearly rent of $2 on each of such leases".
-- Preamble: the 1892 Grant contained "a proviso that if at any time thereafter public worship should cease in the church ... for the
-- space of 2 years, or if such building or buildings should not be maintained thereon or kept in such a state of repair as to fit them
-- for the purposes for which they were built, the said land should forthwith revert to Her Majesty".
--
-- These are recitals of the old instruments, not enacting words. They are encoded because s 6 vests the land subject to the 31 leases
-- and s 7 vests the church land "upon the trusts" of the 1892 Grant, and s 8 saves the rights of the Government; that the reverter
-- still binds the Corporation is an inference from ss 7 and 8, not something the Ordinance says.
GIVEN `number of leases` IS A NUMBER, `rent per lease` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the yearly rent reserved on the building leases` IS
    `number of leases` * `rent per lease`

GIVEN `years public worship has ceased` IS A NUMBER, `the buildings are maintained and kept in repair for their purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recited reverter to the State is triggered` IF
    `years public worship has ceased` >= 2 OR (NOT `the buildings are maintained and kept in repair for their purpose`)

§§ `8 -- whose rights are saved`

-- s 8: "Nothing in this Ordinance shall affect the rights of the Government, or of any bodies politic or corporate, or of other persons
-- than such as are trustees of the said indenture of 14 February 1879, and of the said Statutory Land Grant of 16 August 1892."
--
-- Only the trustees' rights may be affected. s 8 does not also name persons claiming
-- under them.
GIVEN `is a trustee of the 1879 indenture or the 1892 Grant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance may affect their rights` IF
    `is a trustee of the 1879 indenture or the 1892 Grant`
